  "notes": "Where each browser keeps its profiles, used to look for the AI browser extensions listed in ai-tools.json (UA-07, the report and user-status.json). root is under the user's profile folder. engine: chromium (<root>\\<profile>\\Extensions\\<id>\\<version>) or firefox (<root>\\<profile>\\extensions\\<id>.xpi). rootIsProfile: the root is itself a profile as well (older Opera layout). installed: files that show the browser is installed (base programFiles, programFilesX86 or profile), or a Store package installed for the user (appx: the package name, such as Mozilla.Firefox); when none exists, matches are reported as a leftover profile folder, and UA-07 does not count them as a service in use (when one could not be checked, because a folder on the way is a symbolic link an audit run as SYSTEM or elevated does not follow, the browser counts as installed and the skip is reported), so list every place the browser installs to (for Firefox, every edition: Developer Edition, Nightly and the Microsoft Store app keep their profiles in the same folder). programFiles is the 64-bit Program Files folder, also when the audit runs in 32-bit PowerShell. Leave installed out when unsure: the browser then always counts as installed. Only folder and file names are read and no file is opened, so browsing history, cookies, browser settings and extension data are never read. When the audit runs as SYSTEM or elevated, it lists names through a junction below the profile folder only after checking that the junction's target is on this computer, and never through a symbolic link; what it skips is reported (UA-07, and ai.notRead in user-status.json), not dropped. Only extensions listed in ai-tools.json are recorded. To cover another browser with one of these layouts, add an entry; put your copy in %ProgramData%\\EngramicBaseline\\config, where it replaces this one.",
